# What never belongs in a build context.
#
# Keeping this tight is most of the build speed: without it Docker uploads node_modules and
# every .next cache on the machine before the first instruction runs.
#
# **Anchor anything named after a common word.** An unanchored `storage` here matched
# `packages/integrations/src/storage` — the storage driver's own source — and the worker
# built, started, and died on a module it could not find. Every pattern below that is not
# anchored has been checked against the tree for the same mistake.

# Uploaded files when the local storage driver is in use. Anchored, exactly as .gitignore
# anchors them, and for the same reason.
/storage
/apps/*/storage

# Dependencies and build output — reinstalled and rebuilt inside the image.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store
**/.next
**/dist
**/build
**/.turbo

# Secrets. The image takes its configuration from the platform's environment, never from a
# file baked into a layer, where it would survive in the image history.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Generated for pasting into a host's dashboard: real credentials.
/secrets
# Register backups: real names and phone numbers.
/backups

# Local state and tooling noise.
.git
.github
.vercel
.claude
*.log
coverage
playwright-report
test-results
.lighthouseci
tmp

# Not needed to build or run the two services.
apps/kiosk-android
docs
assets
e2e
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.integration.test.ts
